{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775332938-b31y31fEhovlnPshA9Px","role":"assistant","created":1775332952,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me also check if there are any footnotes or markers in the data that might affect the values. Looking at the original data again from page 88 of treasury_bulletin_1980_03:\n\n1979 row (4th group of columns):\n- Jan: 8.43 4/, 9.47\n- Feb: 8.43, 9.52\n- Mar: 8.45, 9.65\n- Apr: 8.44, 9.69\n- May: 8.55 4/5/, 9.82\n- June: 8.32 4/, 9.51\n- July: 8.35, 9.47\n- Aug: 8.42, 9.57\n- Sept: 8.68, 9.87\n- Oct: 9.44 4/, 11.17\n- Nov: 9.80 4/, 11.52\n- Dec: 9.58, 11.30\n\nThe footnotes (4/ and 5/) indicate new bonds added or dropped, but the actual yield values are what we should use.\n\nNow let me verify my calculation once more and write the answer.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_fe91c570fccf470281e3a00f","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# 1979 data - verified from the tables\ntreasury_1979 = [8.43, 8.43, 8.45, 8.44, 8.55, 8.32, 8.35, 8.42, 8.68, 9.44, 9.80, 9.58]\ncorporate_1979 = [9.47, 9.52, 9.65, 9.69, 9.82, 9.51, 9.47, 9.57, 9.87, 11.17, 11.52, 11.30]\n\n# 1984 data - verified from the tables\ntreasury_1984 = [11.82, 12.00, 12.45, 12.65, 13.43, 13.54, 13.36, 12.71, 12.42, 12.04, 11.66, 11.64]\ncorporate_1984 = [12.65, 12.80, 13.36, 13.64, 14.41, 14.49, 14.25, 13.54, 13.37, 13.02, 12.40, 12.47]\n\ndef pearson_correlation(x, y):\n    n = len(x)\n    mean_x = sum(x) / n\n    mean_y = sum(y) / n\n    \n    numerator = sum((x[i] - mean_x) * (y[i] - mean_y) for i in range(n))\n    \n    sum_sq_x = sum((x[i] - mean_x) ** 2 for i in range(n))\n    sum_sq_y = sum((y[i] - mean_y) ** 2 for i in range(n))\n    \n    denominator = math.sqrt(sum_sq_x * sum_sq_y)\n    \n    return numerator / denominator\n\ncorr_1979 = pearson_correlation(treasury_1979, corporate_1979)\ncorr_1984 = pearson_correlation(treasury_1984, corporate_1984)\n\nprint(f\"1979 Pearson correlation: {corr_1979:.10f}\")\nprint(f\"1984 Pearson correlation: {corr_1984:.10f}\")\n\nabs_diff = abs(corr_1979 - corr_1984)\nprint(f\"Absolute difference: {abs_diff:.10f}\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to 4 decimal places: {round(abs_diff, 4)}\")\n\n# The answer should be written without commas or percent signs\nanswer = round(abs_diff, 4)\nprint(f\"\\nFinal answer: {answer}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
